# Sample .http file — ordered from the simplest request to the most advanced.
// Click the "Send Request" / "Copy as curl" CodeLens above each block.
// (httpbin.org echoes back whatever it receives, so you can see the result.)

@baseUrl = https://httpbin.org
@token = dev-secret-123

### 1. The simplest request — just a method and a URL
GET https://httpbin.org/get

### 2. Add a header, and reuse a variable with {{ }}
GET {{baseUrl}}/get?active=true
Accept: application/json

### 3. A POST with headers and an inline JSON body
POST {{baseUrl}}/anything
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "name": "Alice",
  "email": "alice@example.com"
}

### 4. Built-in variables — generated fresh on every send
POST {{baseUrl}}/anything
Content-Type: application/json
X-Request-Id: {{$randomUUID}}

{
  "now": "{{$datetime iso8601}}",
  "rfc1123": "{{$datetime rfc1123}}",
  "yesterday": {{$timestamp -1 d}},
  "dice": {{$randomInt 1 6}},
  "home": "{{$processEnv HOME}}"
}

### 5. Send a body straight from a file (raw — no interpolation)
POST {{baseUrl}}/anything
Content-Type: application/json

< ./payload.json

### 6. Same file, but interpolating {{variables}} inside it before sending
POST {{baseUrl}}/anything
Content-Type: application/json

<@ ./payload.json
